<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Grigorousa	 unloading   sorghum	  14,426     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     15,517</p>
<p>				     corn		7,510</p>
<p>Mecanik Vak	unloading   barley	    3,746     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 186	2/12	 bran		2,550     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 191	2/12	 sunflower meal  2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Yoanis		5/12	 wheat	    34,397     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     24,230</p>
<p>Seagull	     5/12	 maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volzky 32	   7/12	 fodder wheat    3,500     Europe</p>
<p>Antalya	    10/12	 maize grits     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Federal Dora     18/12	 barley+	  25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					feed wheat</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	20/12	 na		 60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Fany		 21/12	 corn+soya+     30,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					wheat</p>
<p>Unity		25/12	 sorghum+corn   50,000     U.S</p>
<p>					gluten+corn</p>
<p>					screening</p>
<p>Auk		  30/12	 na		 40,000     U.S.</p>
